`$before` and `$after` wrap each direct child with a prefix and suffix.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    list #= [$before = [:<li>], $after = [:</li>]:
        <ul>
            [$slot]
        </ul>
    ]
]

This is useful for lists, table rows and repeated layout elements.

Either directive is optional. Values must be compile-time Strings or constant
templates, and may contain named slots but not default or positional slots.
The child insertion point is implicit. Conditions or loops producing no output
do not emit a wrapper; an explicitly selected empty String still does.

Use `$fresh` when one child should skip the immediate wrapper:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [list:
        [: wrapped]
        [$fresh: [: not wrapped]]
    ]
]
